@* Under a photo in a preview, outside the email's block: which photo it is, said as a note for her
   and plainly not part of the email (the walkthrough could not tell whether an italic "Photo: ..."
   caption went out). Where the page knows the library and it has no photo by that name, it says so
   in the same words as the photo field. *@
<p class="field-help" data-photo-note>@Text</p>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ImageRef Image { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>The client's image library, or null where there is none to look in.</summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<LibraryImage>? Library { get; set; }

    private string Text =>
        $"For you, not in the email: the photo \"{Image.Name}\"."
        + (Library is not null && ImageLibrary.Find(Library, Image.Name) is null ? " " + ImageLibrary.NotInLibrary : "");
}
